From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] cuda: cap the MMQ MoE J tile at 64 on sm_121

Port-with-inversion of the R9700 round-7 lever (0023 there). For
mul_mat_id, mul_mat_q_switch_J picks J from ncols_max = n_tokens, landing
at J=128 for prefill batches, while the 256-expert top-8 segments average
~16 columns at ub512. On RDNA4, capping J near the segment width (J=32)
bought +22% prefill by cutting masked-padding work. On the GB10 the same
rule LOSES 9%: sm_121 tensor-core MMQ amortizes per-tile fixed cost over
wide column tiles, so the padding-vs-tile-cost sweet spot sits at J=64,
not at the segment width. Cap the mmid path at the smallest valid config
>= 64 (arch-guarded to sm_121; dense matmuls untouched; decode expert
matvecs route via mmvq, not MMQ). GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_MMQ_MOE_J restores
stock selection.

Measured (runner box gx10-838f, healthy clocks 2405 MHz). Target sweep at
pp512, single process each: 16/32/48/56/64/72/80/96/112/128 read
1597/2101/2272/2375/2370/2358/2352/2350/2328/2297 tok/s; stock-J control
2297-2308. Same-binary toggle A/B, 5 interleaved rounds: pp512 2250-2292
off vs 2350-2372 on, median per-round ratio 1.0332; follow-up 2-round
confirm 2303-2308 -> 2353-2360 (+2.2%). Decode unchanged: tg64 72.4-72.8
both arms (expert decode is mmvq). Gate ppl -c 512 --chunks 8: 3.9306 on
and off, byte-identical, vs stock 3.9322 (-0.04%, band +/-0.5%).
llama-server greedy identity byte-exact off vs on (367-token corpus
prompt, n_predict 64); server-level uncached prefill on that prompt
940.9 -> 986.9 tok/s.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
index 2eb15fd..9fafd5c 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
@@ -1493,6 +1493,35 @@ void mul_mat_q_switch_J(ggml_backend_cuda_context & ctx, const mmq_args & args,
         }
     }

+    // MoE (mul_mat_id) on sm_121: J is otherwise chosen from ncols_max, the
+    // worst-case column count of a single expert segment (= n_tokens for
+    // mul_mat_id), which lands at J=128 for prefill batches. The GB10
+    // tensor-core MMQ measures fastest for the 256-expert top-8 segment mix
+    // at J=56-64: the target sweep 16/32/48/56/64/72/80/96/112/128 read
+    // 1597/2101/2272/2375/2370/2358/2352/2350/2328/2297 pp512 tok/s
+    // (stock-J control 2297-2303). The RDNA4-style near-segment-width cap
+    // (J=32 there, +22% prefill) LOSES 9% here - the tensor cores amortize
+    // per-tile fixed cost over wide tiles, so the sweet spot between that
+    // and masked-padding waste sits at 64, not at the segment width. Toggle
+    // A/B (5 interleaved rounds): pp512 2250-2292 -> 2350-2372, median
+    // per-round ratio 1.0332; decode unchanged (mmvq path, not MMQ).
+    // GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_MMQ_MOE_J restores stock selection.
+    if (args.ids_dst != nullptr && args.nchannels_y > 1 && J_best > 64 &&
+        GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_NVIDIA(cc) && ggml_cuda_highest_compiled_arch(cc) == 1210 &&
+        getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_MMQ_MOE_J") == nullptr) {
+        for (int J = 64; J < J_best; J += 8) {
+            const ggml_cuda_mmq_config config = ggml_cuda_mmq_get_config(type, J, fallback, cc);
+            if (config.type == GGML_TYPE_COUNT) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            if (mmq_get_nbytes_shared(config, cc) > smpbo) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            J_best = J;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+
     switch (J_best) {
         case   8:
             launch_mul_mat_q<type,   8, fallback>(ctx, args, stream);
